# A SQL `GROUP BY` query gets the concrete rewrite to `summarize ... by`.
mode: syntax
---- query
SELECT customerId, count(*) FROM 'orders.csv' GROUP BY customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..66
  PIPELINE@0..65
    ERROR@0..65
      IDENT@0..6 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
      IDENT@7..17 "customerId"
      COMMA@17..18 ","
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      IDENT@19..24 "count"
      L_PAREN@24..25 "("
      STAR@25..26 "*"
      R_PAREN@26..27 ")"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      IDENT@28..32 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
      STRING@33..45 "'orders.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
      IDENT@46..51 "GROUP"
      WHITESPACE@51..52 " "
      IDENT@52..54 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@54..55 " "
      IDENT@55..65 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@65..66 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `SELECT ... FROM` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | SELECT customerId, count(*) FROM 'orders.csv' GROUP BY customerId
  | ^^^^^^                      ---- in DataScript the table comes first
  | |
  | this is SQL
  |
  = help: start with the table and pipe it into operators: `'orders.csv' | summarize count() by customerId`
